"## Summary\n\nAgent-core follow-up 50: members 21's AT02 availability finding, under D-157.\n- **Session:** launched 00:47 EST on 2026-11-04 on #455's roadmap row, and delivered at 02:10. It was resumed at 02:16 to apply the approved F48 change, and finished at 02:27.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 5 commits and 9 owned files, +806/−5. The production change is 100 lines in `node/agent`; the rest is proofs, the fake control server's request history and the dated note.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (after #459) with security-ops 17 and this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/node.mk node-lint`;\n    - `go test ./node/agent/... ./node/internal/fakecontrol/... ./node/watchdog/...`;\n    - the F48, D-157, D-067 and r27 M-1 proofs by name, 23 tests, all passing;\n    - `go vet -tags netlab ./tests/netlab/...`, so the lab compiles;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`, including handover 43's claims, and the committed-evidence tests;\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** one ordinary lab in the lane's own prefix, with no rerun and no reservation. It waited 821 s for other lanes' runs first. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The diagnosis came first (D-141): readiness and D-067's slot are serial prerequisites.**\n  - Central includes members only for a published, registered, ready node with groups. It restores readiness synchronously, in the transaction that accepts the node's clean observation, not in a worker job. A lease request's ACK alone does not make the node ready.\n  - **Rows 557 to 564:**\n    - 557 asked for a lease at 03:30:33.647Z, while still quarantined, and got an empty lease at generation 14;\n    - 558 is the verified closed Apply;\n    - 562 is the heartbeat with `awaiting_member_grants`, and the clean report followed